Generic single-database configuration with an async dbapi.

## Running migrations

The connection string comes from DATABASE_URL in .env (via
app.core.config.get_settings()) -- alembic/env.py reads it and rewrites a
plain postgresql:// URL to postgresql+asyncpg://, the same as the app does.
There is nothing to configure in alembic.ini itself.

Apply all pending migrations (creates research_runs, findings, reports on a
fresh database):

    alembic upgrade head

Create a new migration after changing app/database/models.py:

    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"

Roll back the most recent migration:

    alembic downgrade -1
